    isbefore: []  # 460c
    duplicate_of: []  # 460c
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 460c
    pr_ref:  # 460c
    description: "The Markdown analyzer emits link-target placeholder nodes (representing document-internal references) without emitting any of the document, section, or heading nodes those links should anchor to. The result is a substantial set of orphan link-target nodes that point to nothing in the graph. Separately, on documents that should produce file, section, and heading nodes, the analyzer emits zero such nodes despite processing many markdown files with substantial content. The two halves are complementary: link-targets without anchors, and anchors without links.\n\n### Specific symptoms confirmed on hypergumbo self-analysis\n\n**(1) 102 orphan `external_symbol :doc_link` nodes with zero inbound and zero outbound edges.** The markdown analyzer creates `external_symbol` nodes for relative documentation links (e.g., `adr/0007-...md`, `../audits/0005-...md`). 102 of 105 orphan `<external>` nodes are `markdown:doc_link` with no edges. Same target via different relative paths (`adr/0003-...md`, `docs/adr/0003-...md`, `0003-...md`) creates duplicate nodes — no path canonicalization. The markdown analyzer's doc_link emission and the markdown-link-resolver linker are decoupled: nodes get created but no link edges are emitted, so doc references aren't graph-navigable.\n\n**(2) Zero `file` / `section` / `heading` nodes for 107 analyzed markdown files.** `profile.languages.markdown.files=107` (26,316 LOC). Distinct markdown paths in the `nodes[]` array: 1 (just `<external>`). All 102 markdown-related nodes are `kind=external_symbol` (orphan `:doc_link` from symptom 1). `CHANGELOG.md` (199KB), `CLAUDE.md` (63B), `GEMINI.md` (65B), `docs/hypergumbo-spec.md` all appear in `sketch_precomputed.centrality_scores` with `score=0.0`. `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` do have nonzero centrality (computed from cross-document link inbound counts, which the orphan `:doc_link` nodes provide partially). Effect: `hypergumbo sketch` cannot rank markdown documents by content relevance; `CHANGELOG.md` is invisible to centrality despite being one of the largest documentation files.\n\n### Invariant\n\nA markdown analyzer should emit a coherent set of structural nodes (file, section, heading) with link edges among them. Every link target should resolve to a real node, and every structural node should be reachable. An analyzer that reports `files_analyzed=N` should produce at least one path-bearing node per non-empty input file. The two halves of \"extracts links\" and \"extracts structural nodes\" should be consistent — anchors should match links.\n\n### Scope\n\nAffects every markdown file in the analyzed repository (107 files / 26,316 LOC on hypergumbo self-analysis). 102 orphan link-target nodes (low hundreds), and the same order-of-magnitude missing structural-node count.\n\n### Exposure\n\n`behavior_map.nodes[]` for markdown sources, `sketch_precomputed.centrality_scores` for markdown files, downstream consumers using markdown structure for documentation analysis or doc-link reachability queries.\n\n### Consequence\n\nConsumers using behavior-map data for documentation analysis, doc-link reachability, or section-structure queries get unusable output. Cross-document references cannot be resolved (link targets are orphan nodes). Centrality and ranking views skip markdown content entirely — `CHANGELOG.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `hypergumbo-spec.md` are all `score=0.0` in `sketch_precomputed.centrality_scores`.\n\n### Candidate fixes\n\n- Emit `file` nodes for every markdown file the analyzer processes (one per source file with `files_analyzed>0`).\n- Emit `section` and `heading` nodes for the structural elements within each markdown file; emit edges (`contains`) from `file` → `heading` → `section`.\n- Canonicalize doc-link paths so that `adr/0003-...md`, `docs/adr/0003-...md`, and `0003-...md` resolve to the same target node rather than creating duplicates.\n- Wire the markdown-link-resolver linker to consume the doc_link nodes and emit link edges to the file/section/heading nodes once those are emitted.\n- Add a property test that asserts the markdown analyzer's `files_analyzed` matches the count of distinct `path` values in markdown-origin nodes.\n\n### Subsumed (do not chase)\n\nThis item subsumes INV-zakog, INV-rorug — which are deleted or will be deleted shortly and should only be referenced in an emergency."  # 460c
    fields:  # 460c
      dogfood_anon_id: "ITEM-93e94a"  # 460c
      statement: "A markdown analyzer should emit a coherent set of structural nodes (file, section, heading) with link edges among them. The two halves should be consistent: every link target should resolve, and every structural node should be reachable."  # 460c
      root_cause: "The markdown analyzer emits link-target placeholder nodes (representing document-internal references) without emitting any of the document, section, or heading nodes that those links should be anchored to. The result is a substantial set of orphan link-target nodes that point to nothing in the graph. Separately, on documents that should produce file, section, and heading nodes, the analyzer emits zero such nodes despite processing many markdown files with substantial content. The two halves are complementary aspects of \"the markdown analyzer is broken\" — link-targets without anchors, and anchors without links."  # 460c
