    title: "Markdown --include-docs link resolution: doc links resolve to synthetic <external> (no path canonicalization, no link-resolver); the default-map 'zero file/section nodes' headline is STALE"  # 91cc
    fields:  # 91cc
      statement: "SCOPE (2026-07-21 audit): both default-map HEADLINE symptoms are STALE -- the analyzer DOES emit file + section nodes (markdown.py:185-206; a full docs/adr repro emits 47 file + 1075 section nodes), so 'zero file/section/heading nodes' and 'only orphan :doc_link nodes in the default map' are false. The residual keeping the invariant violated is under opt-in --include-docs: doc links still resolve to synthetic '<external>' placeholders (28 in the repro) rather than real in-repo nodes; _make_link_dst_id (markdown.py:66-84) does NO path canonicalization (adr/0003 vs docs/adr/0003 vs 0003 each duplicate); and no markdown-link-resolver linker module exists. Re-scoped to the --include-docs link-resolution residual."  # 91cc
      root_cause: "CORRECTED 2026-07-21: the earlier 'emits link-target placeholders WITHOUT any document/section/heading nodes' framing is false at HEAD -- file + section nodes ARE emitted (markdown.py:185-206). The real residual: under --include-docs, _make_link_dst_id (markdown.py:66-84) applies no path canonicalization, so doc links resolve to synthetic '<external>' placeholders instead of the real in-repo section/file nodes, and no markdown-link-resolver linker exists to bind them."  # 91cc
